ount again. Compare the historical opening reference, sale profit and settlement chance; A median below the profit floor signals a cost or demand gap. Use the other candidates and market memory when comparable sales are sparse. you may choose another positive price when you explain why. A signed receipt is not a settled sale. Buyer-specific higher quotes are optional experiments ONLY for eligible, market-linked signed identities. Use actual calm high-price settlements under comparable conditions, not a permanent buyer label or an assumed private budget. Unverified/unknown buyers use ordinary evidence. Respect failed or unresolved price probes; never reprice an already agreed receipt. Calculate the ordinary opening quote without anticipating promotions; A public_quote is a binding price ceiling for its physical unit. Prefer a compatible featured unit when useful to the buyer. An explicit quote code narrows the unit choices. a separate tool applies any campaign afterward. Never inflate a base price to offset a discount. Prefer repeatable positive-margin turnover, settled revenue and honest quality over maximizing one markup. Unsold inventory retains acquisition-cost Book credit at round end. Compare selling with holding after storage, spoilage and refund risk; credit is not a cash buyback. Buying inventory does not itself increase Book. Ranking weights are percentiles. Compare receipt_checkout_evidence across available grades. When buyer grades are unspecified and C receipts repeatedly cancel or remain unpaid, consider a profitable A/B alternative before issuing another C receipt. Cancellation can mean private grade, shelf-life or certificate conditions; the exact reason is unknown. Never treat a numeric price as proof of the private checkout policy, invent a policy, mislabel C, or count signatures as paid. C remains available for compatible buyers.", "unit_options": [{"sku": "G476cc094", "unit": "u-64c01276d14c", "grade": "A", "kind": "food", "cost": 18052, "list_pri