e optional experiments ONLY for eligible, market-linked signed identities. Use actual calm high-price settlements under comparable conditions, not a permanent buyer label or an assumed private budget. Unverified/unknown buyers use ordinary evidence. Respect failed or unresolved price probes; never reprice an already agreed receipt. Calculate the ordinary opening quote without anticipating promotions; A public_quote is a binding price ceiling for its physical unit. Prefer a compatible featured unit when useful to the buyer. An explicit quote code narrows the unit choices. a separate tool applies any campaign afterward. Never inflate a base price to offset a discount. Prefer repeatable positive-margin turnover, settled revenue and honest quality over maximizing one markup. Unsold inventory retains acquisition-cost Book credit at round end. Compare selling with holding after storage, spoilage and refund risk; credit is not a cash buyback. Buying inventory does not itself increase Book. Ranking weights are percentiles. Compare receipt_checkout_evidence across available grades. When buyer grades are unspecified and C receipts repeatedly cancel or remain unpaid, consider a profitable A/B alternative before issuing another C receipt. Cancellation can mean private grade, shelf-life or certificate conditions; the exact reason is unknown. Never treat a numeric price as proof of the private checkout policy, invent a policy, mislabel C, or count signatures as paid. C remains available for compatible buyers.", "unit_options": [{"sku": "G08af743b", "unit": "u-d129c16c5195", "grade": "B", "kind": "food", "cost": 6461, "list_price": 14310, "hours_left": 529.1, "storage_per_day": 0.0, "warranty": {"warranty_hours": 0, "refund_share_scenario": 0.0, "risk_source": "operator stress scenario; true breakage probability is unpublished", "estimated_accrued_holding": 0.0, "price_floor": 0}, "book": {"current_stock_credit": 6461, "credit_if_unsold_at_round_end": 6461, "estimated_future_holdi